  "member_id": "pearce-mark",
  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B033",
        "laureates": [
          "Jocelyn Bell Burnell"
        ],
        "citation": "for the discovery of pulsars"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B001",
    "B039"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged. B033 remains the clearest discrete discovery before us: pulsars opened a durable observational domain for neutron stars, gravity, stellar evolution, and plasma physics, and the phenomenon has been extensively and independently confirmed over decades. Bell Burnell's recognition of the anomalous signal provides an unusually direct connection between an individual scientist and the discovery. The round-1 exchange reinforces that maturity and decisive attribution must be assessed separately: the wider observing programme warrants accurate historical treatment, but does not by itself displace her central discovery role.",
    "case_against": "The unresolved historical issue remains substantial. The original observation depended on a supervised programme, instrumentation, and a broader institutional setting; a final citation and public account must accurately state Bell Burnell's decisive contribution without implying that she alone created every condition for the observation. The discussion supplies no archival resolution of that question, so it remains a necessary final review rather than a reason to substitute an achievement with its own unresolved allocation problem.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "danielsson-ulf",
        "point": "Danielsson argues that Bell Burnell's recognition of the anomalous signal is unusually directly attributable, while warning that the wider observing programme must not be obscured.",
        "response": "I agree with both parts of this assessment. The proper standard is not whether a discovery occurred without collaborators or infrastructure, but whether the proposed laureate made the decisive intellectual and observational contribution. B033 meets that standard provisionally; historical review should make the surrounding programme visible without diluting the precise attribution of the discovery."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "eriksson-olle",
        "point": "Eriksson regards B001 as a mature, field-changing conversion of electron microscopy into a quantitative atomic-scale probe, but identifies a diffuse technical lineage and unresolved allocation among Rose, Haider, Krivanek, and other pioneers.",
        "response": "B001 remains my leading experimental alternative because it represents exactly the kind of reproducible instrumental breakthrough that changes what physics can measure. But its unresolved question is more than citation polish: the proposed three names must be shown to capture the indispensable theoretical and practical steps amid several correction concepts and implementations. Until that allocation is settled, B033 offers the more securely delimited final configuration."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "mehlig-bernhard",
        "point": "Mehlig supports B039 as a foundational, experimentally established insight into observable quantum phase, while cautioning that the Aharonov-Bohm effect and Berry phase have distinct histories and mechanisms.",
        "response": "I accept the depth and maturity of B039 and retain it as an alternative. Its proposed unification, however, still requires a citation that says what the two phenomena share without treating them as the same discovery or overlooking other indispensable contributors. That unresolved framing is material when compared with the singular observational discovery in B033."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether historical review can document a public account of Bell Burnell's decisive role that accurately represents the broader pulsar observing programme.",
      "Whether B001's proposed three-person allocation survives archival review of the distinct correction concepts and practical implementations.",
      "Whether B039 can be cited as one coherent achievement while preserving the distinct histories of the Aharonov-Bohm effect and Berry phase."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "None apparent from the supplied profile."
  }
}
